1
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:34,990
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,890
[Episode 9]

3
00:01:38,310 --> 00:01:39,310
We're here, miss.

4
00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:40,720
Careful.

5
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,330
Miss, that's 2 yuan.

6
00:01:43,759 --> 00:01:45,020
I don't have any money.

7
00:01:45,150 --> 00:01:45,950
Come on, miss.

8
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,509
I pulled you all this way.

9
00:01:47,509 --> 00:01:49,090
How can you not pay?

10
00:01:49,110 --> 00:01:50,390
I just don't have any.

11
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:51,590
You just got back?

12
00:01:53,759 --> 00:01:54,490
He has money.

13
00:01:54,759 --> 00:01:55,640
Ask him for it.

14
00:01:56,710 --> 00:01:57,030
Here.

15
00:01:57,030 --> 00:01:57,960
He owes me money.

16
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:58,920
Thank you.

17
00:01:59,039 --> 00:01:59,870
Alright, as long as someone pays.

18
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:01,070
Why did you drink that much?

19
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:03,000
Xin Xiang! Xin Xiang!

20
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,420
What are you doing? Come here.

21
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:06,360
Boss.

22
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,960
Why did she drink so much?

23
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:10,750
Where did you go?

24
00:02:12,030 --> 00:02:14,290
Young Master Feng didn't give you a ride?

25
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:16,840
I just went to Qibao Town in Songjiang.

26
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,370
I didn't take him with me.

27
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:20,690
How come you've started gambling now?

28
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,590
Don't you want to save people?

29
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:24,630
Do you think saving people
doesn't cost money?

30
00:02:24,630 --> 00:02:26,960
One after another, people come
begging me for help.

31
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:29,160
Do they think any of that comes for free?

32
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,180
But can you even win any money?

33
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:34,000
You lost so badly you didn't even
have enough left for a rickshaw ride.

34
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,079
Who do you think you're looking down on?

35
00:02:36,079 --> 00:02:37,680
Next time you go to Qibao Town,

36
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,800
remember to take me along.

37
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:41,150
I'm even better at rolling dice
than taking pictures.

38
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:41,910
Get lost.

39
00:02:48,190 --> 00:02:49,079
Chen.

40
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,120
Aren't you annoying?

41
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:54,680
You have to meddle in everyone's business.

42
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:56,800
You,

43
00:02:58,470 --> 00:02:59,190
come here.

44
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:02,110
Let me show you something great.

45
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,560
Alright, take it.

46
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:18,710
Take it.

47
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:21,310
It's all yours.

48
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:24,680
What do I need this for?

49
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:27,079
To save your beloved cousin.

50
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:29,520
In this world,

51
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:32,870
you can't do anything without money.

52
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:34,730
Good thing you met me.

53
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,360
I told you already,

54
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,300
I don't need you to help me like this.

55
00:03:40,829 --> 00:03:42,690
I'll never be able to pay you back.

56
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:47,590
I'd rather you owe me

57
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,190
than ignore me.

58
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:56,510
And I definitely don't want you
to be unhappy.

59
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:01,650
Money's just a bastard.

60
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:03,610
I can't care about it less.

61
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,360
Money isn't a bastard.

62
00:04:12,150 --> 00:04:13,400
I am.

63
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:15,750
I think

64
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,800
you're one of

65
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,459
the best people in this world.

66
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:24,140
Whoever it is you're trying to save,

67
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:26,070
whatever their identity,

68
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:27,560
I'll support you.

69
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:38,330
Now there's no way to save her
even if I want to.

70
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:42,070
Where there's money, there's a way.

71
00:04:43,159 --> 00:04:44,950
If only it were that simple.

72
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,690
Then what else can I do to help you?

73
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,670
Before I change my mind,

74
00:04:54,390 --> 00:04:55,520
hurry up and tell me.

75
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:00,530
How about you teach me how to dance?

76
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:03,670
Why do you want to learn to dance?

77
00:05:05,070 --> 00:05:06,310
If I can dance,

78
00:05:07,630 --> 00:05:08,950
maybe I can save her.

79
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:14,200
Dancing's my specialty.

80
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,160
Come here.

81
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:26,790
Put your arm around my waist.

82
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:29,950
Let's go.

83
00:05:45,409 --> 00:05:47,290
[Newsstand]

84
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,630
Newspapers for sale! Newspapers for sale!

85
00:05:47,630 --> 00:05:49,470
-Want to buy cigarettes?
-Come check it out.

86
00:05:49,470 --> 00:05:50,350
Newspapers.

87
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:57,840
Want to buy cigarettes, sir?

88
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:14,620
Here.

89
00:06:18,310 --> 00:06:19,940
I was worried it might draw attention,

90
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:21,120
so I bought a few different kinds.

91
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,850
It looks more natural that way.

92
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:24,800
Smart.

93
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:33,930
[Missing Person Notice]

94
00:06:57,830 --> 00:06:59,230
Well, I'll head back now.

95
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,480
You don't have to come every day.

96
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:04,470
It might arouse suspicion.

97
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:07,360
I'll come back after closing tonight.

98
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,820
If you don't get back soon,

99
00:07:09,270 --> 00:07:11,930
the photo studio will have to
shut down for good.

100
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:13,520
I'm off.

101
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,830
Any big news?

102
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:29,610
A female Communist at Renji Hospital
was abducted,

103
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:32,210
and the Labor Union's protest
has died down.

104
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:36,280
Does that count as big news?

105
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:40,640
They've passed judgment on you.

106
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:48,840
Last time, you said you could
send me to Yan'an.

107
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,940
There's no place for me
in Shanghai anymore.

108
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,730
I've made up my mind.

109
00:07:58,159 --> 00:07:59,120
I can go there.

110
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:01,990
At least there,

111
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:04,150
no one will try to kill me.

112
00:08:07,270 --> 00:08:08,240
Are you sure?

113
00:08:12,810 --> 00:08:14,940
Alright, I'll make the arrangements.

114
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:18,480
Thank you.

115
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:30,270
Comrade,

116
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,220
let's shake hands.

117
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,390
Have a safe trip.

118
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:44,550
Let's go.

119
00:09:04,390 --> 00:09:05,120
Where is she?

120
00:09:07,750 --> 00:09:08,810
Where's my cousin?

121
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:11,470
She just left.

122
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:15,620
The higher-ups sent someone
to take her away.

123
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:18,940
Why didn't she wait for me?

124
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:23,550
It was the higher-ups' decision.

125
00:09:23,550 --> 00:09:26,280
She needed to be transferred
as soon as possible.

126
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,840
You should have told me beforehand.

127
00:09:29,270 --> 00:09:31,670
I'm Shen Kexi's family, after all.

128
00:09:43,390 --> 00:09:45,190
Did she leave any message for me?

129
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,320
She said

130
00:09:49,870 --> 00:09:52,240
you might meet again someday.

131
00:09:55,630 --> 00:09:57,160
How could we possibly meet?

132
00:09:58,320 --> 00:09:59,520
She's gone to Yan'an,

133
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:00,750
and I'm in Shanghai.

134
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:03,680
We're in two different worlds now.

135
00:10:05,550 --> 00:10:07,240
So stop telling others

136
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,700
about your relationship.

137
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,750
Tell me the truth.

138
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,540
Is she really safe?

139
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,320
Kailai.

140
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:23,840
Just keep the past
buried deep in your heart

141
00:10:24,550 --> 00:10:25,480
and look ahead.

142
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,480
I'll say the same thing I said before:

143
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:34,480
in Shanghai, it's important
to have the right mentor.

144
00:10:35,150 --> 00:10:36,280
You have to trust me.

145
00:12:05,270 --> 00:12:06,270
Come on. Here.

146
00:12:19,670 --> 00:12:20,390
The phone.

147
00:12:28,510 --> 00:12:29,150
Director.

148
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:32,550
I saw Su Men dancing with
Detective Hua Liang.

149
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:36,440
She's gotten cozy with
the French Concession crowd too?

150
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,530
Yeah, that woman's got some skills.

151
00:12:40,390 --> 00:12:44,190
You don't think she can actually
find that female Communist, do you?

152
00:12:44,230 --> 00:12:45,960
If she really can pull that off,

153
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,460
I'll take my hat off to her.

154
00:12:59,030 --> 00:13:00,430
Miss Shen, you're awake.

155
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:04,150
It might be the side effect
of the painkillers

156
00:13:04,150 --> 00:13:05,880
that made you sleep for so long.

157
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,010
Who are you guys?

158
00:13:11,390 --> 00:13:12,720
His name is Wang Minzhi.

159
00:13:13,030 --> 00:13:14,720
And I'm his wife, Liu Qing.

160
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,500
Where are we going?

161
00:13:25,910 --> 00:13:27,270
Since you've been exposed,

162
00:13:27,270 --> 00:13:29,600
it's not safe to stay in Shanghai anymore.

163
00:13:29,870 --> 00:13:32,870
Come to our station in southern Jiangsu
with us first.

164
00:13:33,030 --> 00:13:35,090
Once we get there, if you are willing,

165
00:13:35,150 --> 00:13:37,210
we'll arrange for you to go to Yan'an.

166
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,450
I'm not a Communist.

167
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,800
Whatever your affiliation,

168
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,670
it's no small feat to survive

169
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,040
such brutal torture.

170
00:13:55,150 --> 00:13:56,810
Seeing the wounds on your feet

171
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:57,770
breaks my heart.

172
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:02,500
These have been difficult times

173
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:03,430
for everyone.

174
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:07,020
There's been a traitor
in the organization.

175
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:10,240
The "Sparrow" operation in Shanghai
nearly got exposed.

176
00:14:10,910 --> 00:14:12,240
The station in Hangzhou

177
00:14:13,670 --> 00:14:15,530
has been betrayed by the traitor.

178
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:19,270
The intelligence networks
in southern Jiangsu and northern Zhejiang

179
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:20,870
have completely collapsed.

180
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,930
It hasn't been easy for any of us

181
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,020
to make it this far.

182
00:14:28,810 --> 00:14:29,970
How could this be?

183
00:14:34,150 --> 00:14:35,200
Everyone's been

184
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:37,220
exceptionally cautious lately,

185
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:38,680
including your superior.

186
00:14:39,810 --> 00:14:42,740
After asking the Shanghai action team
to rescue you,

187
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:45,010
your superior cut off all contact.

188
00:14:47,270 --> 00:14:49,670
The situation in Shanghai is complicated.

189
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:51,240
For your safety,

190
00:14:52,030 --> 00:14:54,430
we have no choice
but to evacuate you first.

191
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:57,970
You've got it wrong.

192
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:00,750
Mr. Du

193
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:03,490
may not have explained things clearly.

194
00:15:04,750 --> 00:15:06,080
I'm not a Communist,

195
00:15:06,510 --> 00:15:07,970
nor do I have any superior.

196
00:15:10,210 --> 00:15:12,140
I'm just trying to save my own life.

197
00:15:13,750 --> 00:15:14,810
It doesn't matter.

198
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,630
Once we reach the liberated area,

199
00:15:16,630 --> 00:15:17,890
we'll all be comrades.

200
00:15:21,770 --> 00:15:23,170
Are we leaving Shanghai?

201
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:28,640
We still have some driving to do.

202
00:15:32,630 --> 00:15:35,630
Su Causeway must,
before the 27th of this month,

203
00:15:35,870 --> 00:15:38,070
arrive at Jinshanzui Fishing Village.

204
00:15:39,550 --> 00:15:40,480
Miss Shen,

205
00:15:41,030 --> 00:15:44,750
is there anything in Shanghai
you can't bear to leave behind?

206
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:50,040
Before we leave Shanghai,

207
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,200
I need to see someone.

208
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:55,320
Who?

209
00:15:57,090 --> 00:15:58,950
Someone I absolutely have to see.

210
00:16:00,030 --> 00:16:01,760
You should have told us sooner.

211
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:04,130
It's very risky to stay in Shanghai

212
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:05,390
any longer.

213
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,150
You should understand

214
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:09,600
how important this is.

215
00:16:13,790 --> 00:16:14,670
Where is it?

216
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,320
We need to hurry.

217
00:16:20,850 --> 00:16:21,850
Jinshanzui

218
00:16:23,670 --> 00:16:24,670
Fishing Village.

219
00:16:32,140 --> 00:16:32,850
Boss.

220
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:35,570
You've been reading this newspaper
for a while.

221
00:16:35,570 --> 00:16:36,960
Is there any major news?

222
00:16:39,510 --> 00:16:40,640
Today at Fairy Bath,

223
00:16:40,670 --> 00:16:42,480
did anything special happen?

224
00:16:45,390 --> 00:16:46,720
I actually have no idea.

225
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:56,820
Why did she leave without saying a word?

226
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:07,010
[Jinshanzui Fishing Village]

227
00:18:01,450 --> 00:18:02,450
Where are we?

228
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:05,640
This is one of our secret safe houses.

229
00:18:05,790 --> 00:18:07,030
We've been driving north

230
00:18:07,030 --> 00:18:08,480
this whole time.

231
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,820
The Jinshanzui Fishing Village
you want to go to

232
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:12,740
is to the south.

233
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,200
It's still a bit far.

234
00:18:15,230 --> 00:18:15,920
Let's take a break here

235
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:16,920
for a bit.

236
00:18:16,950 --> 00:18:18,410
I'll carry you down first.

237
00:18:29,350 --> 00:18:30,610
Since you're injured,

238
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,140
we dare not drive too fast.

239
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:33,880
I'm okay.

240
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:35,780
Rest here for a while.

241
00:18:36,110 --> 00:18:38,370
I'll go get something to eat from the car.

242
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:52,980
I'll get you a bowl of water first.

243
00:19:02,790 --> 00:19:03,480
What is it?

244
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,600
Special Commissioner No. 1 called.

245
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:06,200
Go ahead.

246
00:19:06,750 --> 00:19:08,350
Today at Jinshanzui Fishing Village,

247
00:19:08,350 --> 00:19:10,480
there will be a Communist rendezvous.

248
00:19:11,230 --> 00:19:12,950
Wake up Bi Zhongliang
from the Operations Division

249
00:19:12,950 --> 00:19:14,560
and send people over immediately.
Be quick.

250
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:15,160
Yes.

251
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:25,990
Hurry up, everyone! Hurry up!

252
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:29,260
Hurry up! Move!

253
00:19:29,940 --> 00:19:31,350
Hurry up! Come on!

254
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:36,640
Get in the trucks quickly! Let's go!

255
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:01,100
Li Moqun assigned a special mission.

256
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:02,830
He didn't specify the details.

257
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:06,200
I have a bad feeling—

258
00:20:06,750 --> 00:20:08,880
something's happened to Su Causeway.

259
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:10,320
Drive to Jinshanzui.

260
00:20:10,550 --> 00:20:11,760
You must get there before they do

261
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:13,270
and notify Uncle Hai and the others
to leave.

262
00:20:13,270 --> 00:20:13,720
Got it.

263
00:20:39,830 --> 00:20:41,690
Mr. Wang has been gone for so long.

264
00:20:42,560 --> 00:20:43,960
Should we go check on him?

265
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:45,500
He should be back soon.

266
00:20:46,210 --> 00:20:48,690
Here, have a bowl of water
to warm up first.

267
00:20:50,130 --> 00:20:51,040
Mrs. Wang.

268
00:20:53,830 --> 00:20:54,790
I feel so cold.

269
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:56,480
You feel cold?

270
00:20:58,640 --> 00:20:59,310
Here.

271
00:21:00,110 --> 00:21:01,030
Put this on.

272
00:21:02,310 --> 00:21:03,230
Take my jacket.

273
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:52,880
You're an admirable young lady.

274
00:22:55,110 --> 00:22:56,440
But my orders are clear:

275
00:22:56,990 --> 00:22:59,250
once you tell us where the rendezvous is,

276
00:22:59,510 --> 00:23:00,960
I can send you on your way.

277
00:23:05,420 --> 00:23:06,210
What a pity.

278
00:23:36,510 --> 00:23:37,660
They just left.

279
00:23:38,790 --> 00:23:39,350
Let's go!

280
00:24:04,350 --> 00:24:05,750
Any news on Su Causeway?

281
00:24:06,510 --> 00:24:07,110
Not yet.

282
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:18,560
I only received word

283
00:24:19,070 --> 00:24:21,750
to round up a few men

284
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:24,830
and break a female Communist prisoner
out of the hospital.

285
00:24:24,830 --> 00:24:25,830
Who sent you?

286
00:24:27,830 --> 00:24:29,030
It was Chief Cleaner.

287
00:24:32,550 --> 00:24:33,550
He promised

288
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:35,440
that once the job was done,

289
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:37,590
he'd get all of us into No. 76.

290
00:24:39,590 --> 00:24:40,960
This Cleaner—

291
00:24:42,030 --> 00:24:45,160
I remember he's Director Li's
right-hand man, isn't he?

292
00:24:48,790 --> 00:24:50,850
Your own people broke a fugitive out,

293
00:24:51,210 --> 00:24:53,010
and then pinned the blame on me—

294
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:57,010
Director Li, do you want me dead
or something?

295
00:24:57,530 --> 00:24:59,460
Inspector Su, you misunderstood.

296
00:25:00,510 --> 00:25:03,000
This was actually a setup by Cleaner.

297
00:25:03,600 --> 00:25:04,510
What trap?

298
00:25:12,320 --> 00:25:13,710
Take him away first.

299
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:20,680
Sir!

300
00:25:21,590 --> 00:25:22,270
Sir!

301
00:25:22,520 --> 00:25:24,570
I was just following orders, sir!

302
00:25:28,350 --> 00:25:29,030
General.

303
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,930
I only found out a couple of days ago

304
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:35,790
that Cleaner, in order to confirm
Shen Kexi's affiliation

305
00:25:35,790 --> 00:25:38,310
and get useful information out of her
as quickly as possible,

306
00:25:38,310 --> 00:25:41,310
disguised himself as a Communist
and staged her rescue.

307
00:25:41,310 --> 00:25:43,960
I'm sorry you were caught
in the crossfire, Inspector Su.

308
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:45,690
It was an unfortunate mistake.

309
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:48,280
An unfortunate mistake?

310
00:25:49,800 --> 00:25:51,530
If I hadn't managed to find him,

311
00:25:52,790 --> 00:25:53,550
I'd probably

312
00:25:53,550 --> 00:25:55,500
be on my way back to Nanjing by now,

313
00:25:57,110 --> 00:25:58,910
with this whole mess pinned on me

314
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:00,860
and no way to clear my name.

315
00:26:02,550 --> 00:26:05,310
Inspector Su, you've been wronged.

316
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:14,790
I'd like to apologize to you
on Cleaner's behalf.

317
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:19,540
Everything No. 76 does is for the sake of
gathering intelligence.

318
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:21,800
Inspector Su, we ask for
your understanding

319
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:24,330
regarding the unintended harm
caused to you.

320
00:26:26,300 --> 00:26:28,960
Did you really not know about this,
Director Li?

321
00:26:29,030 --> 00:26:29,680
I didn't.

322
00:26:33,370 --> 00:26:36,630
Your trusted man went behind your back
and acted on his own.

323
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:40,740
I don't see any reason to keep him around.

324
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:43,120
Although Cleaner

325
00:26:43,140 --> 00:26:44,770
handled this matter poorly,

326
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:48,210
his competence and loyalty
are beyond question.

327
00:26:49,030 --> 00:26:50,240
Through this operation,

328
00:26:50,240 --> 00:26:51,640
Cleaner confirmed

329
00:26:51,640 --> 00:26:53,270
that Shen Kexi is a Communist.

330
00:26:53,270 --> 00:26:54,200
At the same time,

331
00:26:54,400 --> 00:26:55,680
we discovered

332
00:26:55,960 --> 00:26:58,030
a secret Communist Party hideout

333
00:26:58,590 --> 00:27:00,390
in Jinshanzui Fishing Village.

334
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:04,440
Did you catch anyone?

335
00:27:05,550 --> 00:27:07,350
Unfortunately, we got there
a bit too late.

336
00:27:07,350 --> 00:27:08,750
The Communists got away.

337
00:27:11,360 --> 00:27:12,560
What about Shen Kexi?

338
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:14,530
She was shot dead by our men.

339
00:27:17,950 --> 00:27:19,300
So after all that,

340
00:27:19,570 --> 00:27:21,770
we didn't get any useful intelligence.

341
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:25,480
Apart from framing me,

342
00:27:26,190 --> 00:27:28,250
this Cleaner hasn't been of much use.

343
00:27:30,480 --> 00:27:31,740
He failed in his duties

344
00:27:32,550 --> 00:27:34,150
and deserves to be punished.

345
00:27:34,740 --> 00:27:35,430
General.

346
00:27:36,680 --> 00:27:38,030
I received word today

347
00:27:39,120 --> 00:27:40,750
that Cleaner has discovered

348
00:27:40,780 --> 00:27:44,160
that those who assassinated Dr. Hoshino
at the racecourse were NBIS agents.

349
00:27:44,160 --> 00:27:46,890
Please give him a chance
to atone for his mistake.

350
00:27:47,350 --> 00:27:49,640
Shen Kexi is just a small fry.

351
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:52,510
The intelligence Cleaner has gathered

352
00:27:52,510 --> 00:27:53,630
is enough to wipe out

353
00:27:53,630 --> 00:27:55,890
the entire NBIS spy network in Shanghai.

354
00:27:56,030 --> 00:27:57,590
The heads of all 12 stations

355
00:27:57,990 --> 00:27:59,250
will show themselves.

356
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:02,270
Really?

357
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:04,960
The operation is already underway.

358
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:19,450
Care for a song, sir?

359
00:28:19,920 --> 00:28:21,310
Care for a song, miss?

360
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:29,650
You're making a fortune today, Auntie.

361
00:28:29,830 --> 00:28:31,510
Business is booming.

362
00:28:32,660 --> 00:28:34,620
You're such a sweet talker now.

363
00:28:35,110 --> 00:28:36,770
I'm starting to like you a bit.

364
00:28:39,170 --> 00:28:40,700
You'd better hurry up then.

365
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:42,750
Life is short.

366
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:46,270
Mutual affection is a great joy.

367
00:28:56,850 --> 00:28:58,520
Wishing you prosperity, sir.

368
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:01,480
What song would you like to hear?

369
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:03,080
"Ambush from All Sides."

370
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:13,750
Quite fitting.

371
00:30:16,790 --> 00:30:20,720
I didn't know you could play that song
on a three-stringed instrument.

372
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:21,830
Quite a turnout.

373
00:31:23,090 --> 00:31:24,890
Just wait to collect the bodies.

374
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:44,160
Where are you going, Auntie?

375
00:31:46,590 --> 00:31:48,270
Are you the boss or am I?

376
00:32:28,260 --> 00:32:29,260
Twelve in total—

377
00:32:30,290 --> 00:32:31,820
don't leave anyone behind.

378
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:43,160
Don't be nervous.

379
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:45,350
The best is yet to come.

380
00:32:46,670 --> 00:32:47,360
Attack!

381
00:32:52,310 --> 00:32:52,920
General.

382
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:01,650
Before you go looking for trouble,

383
00:33:01,650 --> 00:33:02,970
think about how many lives you have.

384
00:33:02,970 --> 00:33:03,610
Move!

385
00:33:12,260 --> 00:33:13,060
Inspector Su.

386
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:22,680
This is a day worth celebrating.

387
00:34:40,030 --> 00:34:41,320
How could you lie to me?

388
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:46,440
I was going to save you for last.

389
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:12,070
Put them all in the truck ahead.

390
00:35:12,070 --> 00:35:12,670
Move!

391
00:35:18,600 --> 00:35:19,330
Director Li.

392
00:35:21,700 --> 00:35:24,010
That was a beautiful fight.

393
00:35:33,640 --> 00:35:35,100
Life really is like a play.

394
00:35:35,760 --> 00:35:38,160
It all comes down to
who's the better actor.

395
00:35:42,200 --> 00:35:43,720
You're the expert.

396
00:35:44,400 --> 00:35:46,060
You really put on a great show.

397
00:36:24,400 --> 00:36:25,320
It's Auntie.

398
00:36:25,920 --> 00:36:26,840
It's Auntie!

399
00:36:27,510 --> 00:36:28,400
Auntie!

400
00:36:29,030 --> 00:36:30,030
Auntie!

401
00:36:30,670 --> 00:36:31,600
Auntie!

402
00:36:33,320 --> 00:36:34,590
Let go of me!

403
00:36:42,730 --> 00:36:43,850
Let go of me!

404
00:36:45,550 --> 00:36:46,960
It's Auntie!

405
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:56,970
Did you bring an axe?

406
00:36:58,070 --> 00:36:59,730
If you have to, just cut it off.

407
00:37:00,450 --> 00:37:01,220
Got it.

408
00:37:09,030 --> 00:37:10,030
Du Huangqiao!

409
00:37:10,310 --> 00:37:11,620
You bastard!

410
00:37:11,740 --> 00:37:13,050
I'll kill you!

411
00:37:14,480 --> 00:37:15,840
You're from No. 76.

412
00:37:21,320 --> 00:37:23,920
Didn't you say you wanted to
save this country?

413
00:37:45,590 --> 00:37:46,920
So you're Cleaner?

414
00:37:47,370 --> 00:37:49,120
You scared the hell out of me.

415
00:37:51,200 --> 00:37:52,960
It couldn't be that bad, Mr. Zhao.

416
00:37:52,960 --> 00:37:54,220
I'll be counting on you

417
00:37:55,380 --> 00:37:57,020
to look out for me from now on.

418
00:37:57,440 --> 00:37:58,800
Me, look out for you?

419
00:37:59,150 --> 00:38:01,590
From now on, I'd better
learn how to tell fortunes too.

420
00:38:01,590 --> 00:38:02,440
In this world,

421
00:38:02,670 --> 00:38:04,470
the blind are the most ruthless.

422
00:38:15,670 --> 00:38:16,440
Fall in!

423
00:39:02,710 --> 00:39:03,840
Get some rest early.

424
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:07,760
I want to make more money.

425
00:39:08,800 --> 00:39:09,470
What?

426
00:39:10,840 --> 00:39:12,280
Lots and lots of money.

427
00:39:17,490 --> 00:39:19,750
What's the point of making so much money?

428
00:39:23,840 --> 00:39:25,240
Once we've saved enough,

429
00:39:27,280 --> 00:39:28,880
let's move back to Hangzhou.

430
00:39:31,800 --> 00:39:34,030
I don't want to end up like Auntie,

431
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:38,660
leaving behind nothing but a cloth shoe.

432
00:39:42,800 --> 00:39:44,280
I just can't make it out—

433
00:39:45,400 --> 00:39:47,710
how could Auntie have been from the NBIS?

434
00:39:51,880 --> 00:39:53,630
Does everyone have secrets?

435
00:39:58,960 --> 00:39:59,880
Chen.

436
00:40:03,490 --> 00:40:05,550
Are you hiding something from me too?

437
00:40:06,460 --> 00:40:07,950
Auntie was from the NBIS,

438
00:40:10,800 --> 00:40:12,460
and Du Huangqiao is a traitor.

439
00:40:16,480 --> 00:40:17,630
Then what are you?

440
00:40:20,150 --> 00:40:21,320
Tell me the truth.

441
00:40:21,970 --> 00:40:24,450
I... I'm a photographer.

442
00:40:27,410 --> 00:40:28,410
No. That's not it.

443
00:40:30,670 --> 00:40:32,550
You've been going to Fairy Bath
for no reason

444
00:40:32,550 --> 00:40:33,680
these past few days.

445
00:40:36,960 --> 00:40:38,760
What exactly have you been up to?

446
00:40:46,840 --> 00:40:48,190
I went to see my cousin.

447
00:40:53,280 --> 00:40:54,550
She was at Fairy Bath?

448
00:40:55,440 --> 00:40:58,150
Du Huangqiao disguised himself
as a Communist,

449
00:40:59,150 --> 00:41:00,810
broke her out of the hospital,

450
00:41:02,030 --> 00:41:03,630
and hid her in the bathhouse.

451
00:41:06,360 --> 00:41:07,890
Why didn't you tell me about

452
00:41:09,070 --> 00:41:10,470
something this serious?

453
00:41:11,390 --> 00:41:13,950
The more people who know,
the greater the danger.

454
00:41:13,950 --> 00:41:15,480
I didn't want to drag you into this.

455
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:16,360
Nonsense.

456
00:41:17,670 --> 00:41:19,070
You just don't trust me.

457
00:41:24,590 --> 00:41:27,990
That blind bastard really had you
wrapped around his finger.

458
00:41:33,360 --> 00:41:34,760
Where's your cousin now?

459
00:41:37,070 --> 00:41:38,400
That blind bastard said

460
00:41:38,670 --> 00:41:39,930
she was sent to Yan'an.

461
00:41:44,170 --> 00:41:46,330
More like she was sent to hell.

462
00:41:48,550 --> 00:41:49,360
Impossible.

463
00:41:51,030 --> 00:41:52,830
My cousin's smart and vigilant.

464
00:41:53,070 --> 00:41:54,600
She must've found a way out.

465
00:41:57,280 --> 00:41:58,510
Wasn't Auntie smart?

466
00:41:58,750 --> 00:41:59,950
Wasn't she vigilant?

467
00:42:02,120 --> 00:42:05,450
She was even so nice to that blind bastard
when she was alive.

468
00:42:07,230 --> 00:42:10,290
And in the end, she didn't even
have an intact body left.

469
00:42:16,720 --> 00:42:17,550
Chen.

470
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:21,500
You must promise me

471
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:25,930
that from now on, you'll never
keep anything from me.

472
00:42:31,760 --> 00:42:33,560
We have to stay alive, both of us.

473
00:42:36,360 --> 00:42:38,160
We came from Hangzhou together,

474
00:42:40,800 --> 00:42:42,330
and when it's time to leave,

475
00:42:44,590 --> 00:42:46,070
we'll leave together.

476
00:42:53,850 --> 00:42:54,600
Okay.
